# Copy to .env.local for local development. Never commit .env.local.
#
# Both values come from your Supabase project:
#   Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API keys
#
# Supabase now offers two key systems. Either works here:
#
#   "Publishable and secret API keys"  (preferred — this is the newer system)
#     -> use the PUBLISHABLE key. It starts with sb_publishable_
#
#   "Legacy anon, service_role API keys"
#     -> use the ANON / PUBLIC key. A long JWT starting with eyJ
#
# Whichever you pick, it is meant to be public: it ships in the JavaScript
# bundle and anyone can read it. That is safe because row-level security decides
# what it can actually reach. See supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql.
#
# NEVER use the SECRET key (sb_secret_...) or the SERVICE_ROLE key here.
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is compiled into the client bundle, and those two
# bypass row-level security entirely — publishing one hands over the database.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here
